editorialMd:
The working idea

Jobs arrive together in input order and need the given nonnegative service times. A clerk serves up to k time units, appends unfinished jobs to the queue, and records each job's completion time in original job order. A zero-time job is complete at time 0.

Return the first value in the derived sequence that is at least k, or -1 if there is none. Return the value, not its index.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n + total/k); space O(n).

javascript
function roundDeskFirstQualifyingSlip(readings, k) {
  const a=readings; let out=[];
  const remaining=[...a],queue=[];out=Array(a.length).fill(0);for(let i=0;i<a.length;i++)if(a[i]>0)queue.push(i);let time=0;for(let head=0,tail=queue.length;head<tail;head++){const i=queue[head%a.length],served=Math.min(k,remaining[i]);remaining[i]-=served;time+=served;if(remaining[i])queue[tail++%a.length]=i;else out[i]=time;}
  return out.find(x=>x>=k)??-1;
}


